Id_42 wrote:
> Has anybody written any sort of program to splice together copies of
> the logfile and copies of the records file? (Say, for people who
> played regularly on more than one computer, or for friends who wanted
> to compete with each other on their own machines while still being
> able to easily compare scores.) Just curious.

If you are using WinDOS... - others may help.

On a Unix system you have everything you need on board...


cat record1 record2 ... recordN | sort -nr +1  > record.new

sorts the N record files you listed numerically using the high score
field.

Depending on how many entries you want to keep you may restrict the
output further, say to a size defined by the record file "record1"
(you may have this command on a single line)

cat record1 record2 ... recordN | sort -nr +1 |
   head -n $(wc -l <record1)  > record.new


To collect the logfiles you have to sort the entries using one of the
date fields, e.g.

cat logfile1 logfile2 ... logfileN | sort +8  > logfile.new


